gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip=Machine Type: §eRemote Multiblock Host§r\nRuns connected machines of one type from centralized I/O and energy hatches\nRemote machines remain formed and keep energy hatches only to define voltage, amperage and overclocking\nPut the target machine controller item in this controller slot to select its type\nNormal, multi-amp and laser hatches are supported; all capacity becomes one aggregate recipe\nBatch mode is supported; disabling work finishes the current recipe first; progress is shown in seconds\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§eConnection setup:\n§f1. Form and start a Drone Centre, then put at least one drone in its input bus\n§f2. Replace the maintenance hatch here and on every remote with a Drone DownLink Module\n§f3. Same-dimension links are automatic in range: T1 128, T2 512, T3/T4 4096 blocks\n§f4. With T4, use the same key for infinite/cross-dimension range\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidance
gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip_secondary=§fSize: §63§7x§63§7x§63§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure:\n   §fController: §7Front center\n   §616+ §fZPM Machine Casings\n   §eExactly 1 §fDrone DownLink Module: §7Any casing\n   §e1 exotic or 1-2 normal §fEnergy Hatches (multi-amp/laser supported): §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus/Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus/Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §fAir: §7Center\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f on the controller to visualize/build it!
